<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/19th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Treaty</p><h1 class="enc-title">Anglo-Dutch Treaty of 1824</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1824">1824</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Anglo-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch">Dutch</a> Treaty of 1824 was an agreement between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-the-netherlands">Netherlands</a> that divided their spheres of influence in maritime South-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/east-asia">East Asia</a>. Britain took control of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/malay-peninsula">Malay Peninsula</a>, including <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/malacca">Malacca</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/singapore">Singapore</a>, while the Netherlands kept the islands to the south, including <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sumatra">Sumatra</a>. It defined the boundaries of later Dutch rule in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/east-indies">East Indies</a>.</p></div>
